course: dictionary
lesson: 9283
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one the writer means. «The Elephant's Child was spanked again and again for asking questions.» Here spanking is a punishment. The clue is that he is hit for asking so many questions.
explain: Now read: «They set off at a spanking pace.» A pace is a speed, so spanking must mean fast and lively here. Ask yourself: what word would fit? Put in fast, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Spanking can also come before new, as in «a spanking new bike». This means brand new and shiny. It is an informal phrase, so you will hear it in everyday talk more than in formal writing. Read the words around it to decide which meaning is right.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: As a noun, «spanking» means a punishment of hitting a child's bottom with an open hand.
fact: As an adjective, «spanking» means fast, lively and fine, as in «a spanking breeze».
fact: As an adverb, «spanking» means very, as in «spanking new».
fact: Hitting children is against the law in many countries, including Scotland, Wales, Ireland and New Zealand, and many people think it is wrong.
exercise: «The Elephant's Child was spanked again and again.» What does spanked mean here? | A punishment by hitting with an open hand | Very quiet | Brand new and shiny | *Fast and lively
exercise: «They set off at a spanking pace.» What does spanking mean here? | *Fast, lively and fine | A punishment by hitting | Brand new and shiny | Very quiet
exercise: Mia says her bike is «spanking new». What does spanking mean here? | A punishment for naughty children | *Brand new and shiny | Slow and sad | Old and rusty
test: Which meaning fits «spanking new» in «The shop sold spanking new trainers»? | *Brand new and shiny | Hitting children as a punishment | Very quiet and shy | Fast and lively
test: What does «spanking» mean in «a spanking breeze» on a sunny day at the seaside? | Hitting with an open hand | Very old and worn | Cold and grey | *Fast, fresh and lively
exam: Which check helps you choose the right meaning of spanking? | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Ask someone to guess without reading the sentence | Count the letters in the word | Look only at the first letter
